<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Aram-Zobah</h1><p class="st-meta">1050 BCE – 950 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aram-Zobah, an Aramaean kingdom of the 10th century BCE, the main rival of King David in the Bible.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Zobah was an Aramaean kingdom probably centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beqaa-valley">Beqaa</a> valley and the region north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>. It is known almost entirely from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, which describes its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadadezer-of-zobah">Hadadezer son of Rehob</a> as a powerful ruler whose influence reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Bible</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadadezer-of-zobah">Hadadezer</a> commanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and allied Aramaean kingdoms, and rich towns of his land produced bronze. Little else is known, since no inscriptions from Zobah have been found.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Bible</a> says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-israel">United Kingdom of Israel</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadadezer-of-zobah">Hadadezer</a> and took his gold shields to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, and that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rezon">Rezon</a>, a former officer, founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aram-damascus">Aram-Damascus</a>, which soon replaced Zobah as the leading Aramaean power.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1050 BCE – 950 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:38.81%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1050 BCE – 950 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hadadezer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Aramaean religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aramaic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Syria, Lebanon</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zobah</dd></dl></aside></div>
